1
00:00:00,044 --> 00:00:01,244
This is the thing.
ここが大事なんだけど

2
00:00:01,944 --> 00:00:03,064
You could say all this stuff.
いろいろ言うのはいい

3
00:00:03,084 --> 00:00:05,804
You could say Tuskegee and people
don't even know what that is.
でも「Tuskegee」って言っても
みんな知らないんだよ

4
00:00:05,824 --> 00:00:07,434
Right. Hold on. Hold on.
そうだな
待て待て

5
00:00:07,454 --> 00:00:08,764
No, I know. Hold up.
いや、わかってる
待って

6
00:00:09,074 --> 00:00:12,474
And they just think you're
throwing things out there,
みんな「適当に言ってる」

7
00:00:12,494 --> 00:00:15,274
and they're like, yeah,
he's just saying things.
「口から出まかせだ」って
思っちゃうんだよ

8
00:00:15,294 --> 00:00:19,504
But if people do the research,
if you can articulate what Tuskegee...
でもみんなが調べたら　Tuskegeeで
実際に何があったか説明できたら

9
00:00:19,524 --> 00:00:24,054
what really happened, which
is legit, it really happened,
あれは本当にあったことだから

10
00:00:24,074 --> 00:00:28,824
it's not a conspiracy theory. The
government did this to people.
陰謀論じゃない　政府が実際に
やったことなんだ

11
00:00:29,954 --> 00:00:33,954
Then you can get people on
the side of what you're saying.
そうすれば
みんな味方してくれる

12
00:00:33,974 --> 00:00:40,654
It all becomes about articulation
and history, because history is real.
大事なのは伝え方と歴史
歴史は事実だからな

13
00:00:41,934 --> 00:00:45,934
And that's what I think.
Sometimes I think we as Americans,
俺はそう思う
アメリカ人には

14
00:00:45,954 --> 00:00:47,434
we have no history anymore.
もう歴史がないんじゃないかって

15
00:00:47,454 --> 00:00:50,414
We're not learning
history, real history.
歴史を学んでない
本当の歴史をな

16
00:00:50,434 --> 00:00:53,444
Teaching history,
it's all done, it's gone.
歴史の授業なんて
もう消えちまった

17
00:00:54,334 --> 00:00:58,814
And we need to bring that back,
and bring it back in the right way,
それを取り戻さなきゃ　正しいやり方でな
何が本当にあったか

18
00:00:58,834 --> 00:01:01,054
where people articulate
what really happened.
ちゃんと伝えられるように

19
00:01:02,054 --> 00:01:03,844
What you guys are doing,
what's different right here,
お前らがやってることは
ここが違うんだよ

20
00:01:03,864 --> 00:01:07,024
because as you're talking,
I felt, I was like, wow,
話を聞いてて思った

21
00:01:07,504 --> 00:01:09,594
there wouldn't have been
no way for me to become
「Drink Champsに来なかったら

22
00:01:09,614 --> 00:01:12,174
president without
coming to Drink Champs.
大統領にはなれなかった」って

23
00:01:12,194 --> 00:01:15,904
When you were talking
right now, like...
今の話を聞いてて…

24
00:01:19,184 --> 00:01:23,334
you know, what you...
the way you articulated it,
その伝え方だよ
俺たちがずっと

25
00:01:23,354 --> 00:01:26,644
because it's very important that we
stay in constant communication.
話し合い続けることが
すごく大事なんだ

26
00:01:27,944 --> 00:01:30,494
That's what the
enemy wants us to do.
敵の狙いはそこなんだ

27
00:01:30,514 --> 00:01:32,314
They don't want us to talk.
Like the slave ships, right?
俺たちに話させたくない
奴隷船と同じだよ

28
00:01:32,334 --> 00:01:34,741
They cut our tongues and told
us not to talk to each other.
舌を切って
互いに話すなって言った
